The anti-Goodhart setup is crucial

I'd have four layers:

TRAIN
policy evolution allowed

DEV
hyperparameter decisions allowed

VALIDATION
candidate selection only

SECRET
one-shot final evaluation

And parent claim + every mutation stays in the same split.

Even better, have an evaluator firewall:

Policy being evolved
      X
cannot see:
ground-truth label
FactJudge internals
secret examples

It only sees normal runtime state:

claim
retrieved evidence
provider metadata
confidence

Otherwise Cogym may discover weird lexical exploits of FactJudge.

And I would keep an independent metric based directly on the known dataset labels. FactJudge should produce the runtime verdict; ground truth should score whether the whole system actually succeeded.

That's an important distinction.

